//@version=6
// NQ — Initial Balance (IB) breakout-retracement backtest, Edgeful-style rules
//
// WHAT THIS IS: a clean, mechanical backtest of the Initial Balance strategy that edgeful
// publishes for index futures. It is deliberately small — one setup, one trade a day, no
// indicator stack on top.
//
// THE RULES (as edgeful documents them, see SOURCE NOTES at the bottom of this file):
//   1. Initial Balance = the high and low of the first hour of the NY session, 9:30–10:30 ET.
//   2. Wait for that hour to CLOSE. Nothing is traded while the IB is still forming.
//   3. Wait for a break of the IB high (long bias) or IB low (short bias).
//   4. Do NOT chase the break. Enter on the retracement back INTO the range, at 25% of the
//      IB range inside the broken edge.
//   5. Stop loss at 60% of the IB range, measured from the broken edge (i.e. deeper inside
//      the range than the entry).
//   6. Target 50% of the IB range beyond the broken edge.
//   7. If neither stop nor target is hit, flatten at the end of the session.
//
//   With the defaults that is a fixed geometry: risk = 35% of the IB range, reward = 75% of
//   the IB range → ~2.14R per trade before costs.
//
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// BUILT FOR FUTURES (NQ1! / MNQ1! on CME_MINI). Read this before changing anything:
//
//   • MARGIN — this is the setting that decides whether you get any trades at all.
//     Pine v6 defaults margin_long/margin_short to 100 (%) and, unlike v4, ENFORCES it.
//     NQ at ~24,000 is 24,000 x $20 = ~$480,000 of notional per contract, so at 100%
//     margin a $50,000 account can never afford a single contract and every order is
//     silently cancelled — the Strategy Tester just shows zero trades. This is why an
//     un-margined script "works" on a NAS100 CFD (1 unit ~ $24,000 of notional, which
//     fits) and does nothing on NQ1!. Below it is set to 1%, roughly $4,800 per contract
//     at current prices — conservative next to the $500–$2,000 intraday margin most
//     futures brokers actually charge, and this strategy is flat by 15:55 ET every day so
//     overnight initial margin (~5%) never applies. Raise it in Properties → "Margin for
//     long/short positions %" if you want to model overnight or exchange margin.
//
//   • POINT VALUE is read from the symbol, so P&L is correct automatically:
//     NQ = $20/point, MNQ = $2/point. Only the commission below needs changing for MNQ.
//
//   • PRICES ARE ROUNDED TO THE TICK. NQ ticks are 0.25, and a percentage of the IB range
//     almost never lands on one. Every order price is snapped with math.round_to_mintick().
//
//   • SESSION TIMES ARE WALL-CLOCK NEW YORK, computed from hour()/minute() rather than a
//     session string. Futures sessions roll at 18:00 ET the previous day and the chart's
//     ETH/RTH toggle changes the session definition underneath you; wall-clock comparison
//     is immune to both, and to daylight saving.
//
// NO REPAINTING: the IB is finalised only after the 9:30–10:30 window has closed, every
// level is derived from completed bars, orders are submitted at bar close, and there are no
// higher-timeframe requests. Nothing here can see the future.
//
// TIMEFRAME: run it on 1–5 minute NQ1!. Lower timeframes resolve the intrabar sequence of
// stop-vs-target more honestly. Above 15m the IB window stops being measured cleanly and the
// stats table will warn you.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

strategy(
     title                   = "NQ Initial Balance (Edgeful-style)",
     shorttitle              = "NQ IB",
     overlay                 = true,
     pyramiding              = 0,
     initial_capital         = 50000,
     default_qty_type        = strategy.fixed,
     default_qty_value       = 1,
     commission_type         = strategy.commission.cash_per_contract,
     commission_value        = 2.50,      // ~$5 round turn on NQ. Use ~0.50 for MNQ.
     slippage                = 2,         // ticks per side; NQ tick = 0.25 pt = $5
     margin_long             = 1,         // % of notional — see the MARGIN note above
     margin_short            = 1,
     calc_on_every_tick      = false,
     process_orders_on_close = false)
// All five cost/sizing values above must be compile-time constants in Pine, so they cannot be
// Inputs. Every one of them is editable live in the Strategy Tester's *Properties* tab
// (Order size, Commission, Slippage, Margin), which overrides the code without editing it.

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Inputs
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
TZ = "America/New_York"   // handles EST/EDT automatically

gS = "Session (New York wall-clock)"
ibStartH = input.int(9,  "IB starts — hour",   minval = 0, maxval = 23, group = gS, inline = "a")
ibStartM = input.int(30, ":",                  minval = 0, maxval = 59, group = gS, inline = "a")
ibEndH   = input.int(10, "IB ends — hour",     minval = 0, maxval = 23, group = gS, inline = "b")
ibEndM   = input.int(30, ":",                  minval = 0, maxval = 59, group = gS, inline = "b")
exitH    = input.int(15, "Flatten — hour",     minval = 0, maxval = 23, group = gS, inline = "c")
exitM    = input.int(55, ":",                  minval = 0, maxval = 59, group = gS, inline = "c", tooltip = "Entries are armed from the IB close until this time. At this time any unfilled order is cancelled and any open position is closed.")

gR = "Strategy rules"
retrPct  = input.float(25, "Entry — retracement into IB (% of range)", minval = 0,   maxval = 99,  step = 1,   group = gR, tooltip = "edgeful's documented entry: 25% of the IB range back inside the broken edge.")
stopPct  = input.float(60, "Stop — from broken edge (% of range)",     minval = 1,   maxval = 200, step = 1,   group = gR, tooltip = "edgeful's documented stop: 60% of the IB range measured from the broken edge. Must be larger than the entry retracement.")
useRR    = input.bool(false, "Use fixed R:R target instead of % target",                                       group = gR)
tgtPct   = input.float(50, "Target — beyond broken edge (% of range)", minval = 1,   maxval = 500, step = 1,   group = gR, tooltip = "edgeful's documented target: 50% of the IB range beyond the broken edge.")
rrMult   = input.float(2.0, "Risk : Reward (when fixed R:R is on)",    minval = 0.1, maxval = 20,  step = 0.1, group = gR)
useBE    = input.bool(false, "Move stop to breakeven",                                                        group = gR, tooltip = "edgeful publishes this as a separate 'IB breakeven stop' variant. Off by default so the base rules are measured first.")
bePct    = input.float(25, "Breakeven trigger (% of range beyond edge)", minval = 1, maxval = 500, step = 1,  group = gR)

gF = "Filters"
allowLong  = input.bool(true,  "Allow longs",  group = gF)
allowShort = input.bool(true,  "Allow shorts", group = gF)
minIB      = input.float(0, "Min IB range (points, 0 = off)", minval = 0, step = 5, group = gF, tooltip = "Skips dead first hours where the geometry gives almost no reward.")
maxIB      = input.float(0, "Max IB range (points, 0 = off)", minval = 0, step = 5, group = gF, tooltip = "Skips news-blowout first hours where the 60% stop is enormous.")
allow2nd   = input.bool(false, "Allow a second trade (double-break days)", group = gF, tooltip = "Default off — the documented strategy is one trade per day. On: after the first trade closes, a break of the OPPOSITE side can be traded too.")

gV = "Display"
showLevels = input.bool(true, "Plot IB / entry / stop / target", group = gV)
showTable  = input.bool(true, "Show statistics table",           group = gV)

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Session state — wall-clock New York, independent of the symbol's session definition
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
nyMin = hour(time, TZ) * 60 + minute(time, TZ)
nyDow = dayofweek(time, TZ)
weekday = nyDow != dayofweek.saturday and nyDow != dayofweek.sunday

ibFrom = ibStartH * 60 + ibStartM
ibTo   = ibEndH   * 60 + ibEndM
exitAt = exitH    * 60 + exitM

inIB    = weekday and nyMin >= ibFrom and nyMin < ibTo
inTrade = weekday and nyMin >= ibTo   and nyMin < exitAt

ibStart  = inIB and not inIB[1]           // first bar of the 9:30–10:30 window
ibClosed = not inIB and inIB[1]           // first bar AFTER the window — IB is now final
tradeEnd = not inTrade and inTrade[1]     // first bar after the trade window

var float ibH   = na
var float ibL   = na
var bool  ready = false      // IB finalised for today

var int   dir       = 0      // 0 = no break taken yet, 1 = long taken, -1 = short taken
var int   doneDir   = 0      // sides already used today (so a 'second trade' must be the other side)
var int   tradesDay = 0
var float ePrice    = na
var float sPrice    = na
var float tPrice    = na
var float curStop   = na
var bool  armed     = false  // a resting entry order exists

// Day reset happens on the first bar of the IB window — every level below is rebuilt from
// scratch each session.
if ibStart
    ibH       := high
    ibL       := low
    ready     := false
    dir       := 0
    doneDir   := 0
    tradesDay := 0
    ePrice    := na
    sPrice    := na
    tPrice    := na
    curStop   := na
    armed     := false
else if inIB
    ibH := math.max(ibH, high)
    ibL := math.min(ibL, low)

if ibClosed
    ready := true

ibRange = ready ? ibH - ibL : na

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Setup detection — break, then retracement entry
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
sizeOK  = not na(ibRange) and ibRange > 0 and (minIB <= 0 or ibRange >= minIB) and (maxIB <= 0 or ibRange <= maxIB)
geomOK  = stopPct > retrPct     // otherwise the stop would sit on the wrong side of the entry
canScan = ready and inTrade and dir == 0 and sizeOK and geomOK and strategy.position_size == 0

brokeUp = canScan and high > ibH and doneDir !=  1
brokeDn = canScan and low  < ibL and doneDir != -1

// If a single bar takes out both sides, follow the direction that bar closed in.
goLong  = brokeUp and (not brokeDn or close >= open) and allowLong
goShort = brokeDn and (not brokeUp or close <  open) and allowShort

if goLong
    dir     := 1
    doneDir := 1
    ePrice  := math.round_to_mintick(ibH - ibRange * retrPct / 100)
    sPrice  := math.round_to_mintick(ibH - ibRange * stopPct / 100)
    tPrice  := math.round_to_mintick(useRR ? ePrice + rrMult * (ePrice - sPrice) : ibH + ibRange * tgtPct / 100)
    curStop := sPrice
    armed   := true
    // Resting limit BUY below the market: price must retrace into the IB to fill us.
    strategy.entry("IB Long", strategy.long, limit = ePrice, comment = "IB long")
else if goShort
    dir     := -1
    doneDir := -1
    ePrice  := math.round_to_mintick(ibL + ibRange * retrPct / 100)
    sPrice  := math.round_to_mintick(ibL + ibRange * stopPct / 100)
    tPrice  := math.round_to_mintick(useRR ? ePrice - rrMult * (sPrice - ePrice) : ibL - ibRange * tgtPct / 100)
    curStop := sPrice
    armed   := true
    // Resting limit SELL above the market.
    strategy.entry("IB Short", strategy.short, limit = ePrice, comment = "IB short")
else if brokeUp or brokeDn
    // Break happened but that side is disabled — burn it so we don't flip into the other side.
    dir     := brokeUp ? 1 : -1
    doneDir := dir

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Position management
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
inLong  = strategy.position_size > 0
inShort = strategy.position_size < 0
justFilled = strategy.position_size != 0 and strategy.position_size[1] == 0

if justFilled
    armed     := false
    tradesDay += 1

// Breakeven: once price has run bePct of the range beyond the broken edge, pull the stop to entry.
if useBE and strategy.position_size != 0
    if inLong and high >= ibH + ibRange * bePct / 100
        curStop := math.max(curStop, ePrice)
    if inShort and low <= ibL - ibRange * bePct / 100
        curStop := math.min(curStop, ePrice)

if inLong
    strategy.exit("IB Long X", from_entry = "IB Long", stop = curStop, limit = tPrice, comment_loss = "stop", comment_profit = "target")
if inShort
    strategy.exit("IB Short X", from_entry = "IB Short", stop = curStop, limit = tPrice, comment_loss = "stop", comment_profit = "target")

// Trade closed — allow the opposite break only if the user opted into double-break days.
justClosed = strategy.position_size == 0 and strategy.position_size[1] != 0
if justClosed
    if allow2nd and tradesDay < 2 and inTrade
        dir     := 0
        ePrice  := na
        sPrice  := na
        tPrice  := na
        curStop := na
    else
        armed := false

// End of session — cancel anything unfilled, flatten anything open.
if tradeEnd
    strategy.cancel_all()
    if strategy.position_size != 0
        strategy.close_all(comment = "EOD flat")
    armed := false
    ready := false

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Plots
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
liveDay  = showLevels and (inIB or (ready and inTrade))
liveTrad = showLevels and (armed or strategy.position_size != 0)

plot(liveDay  ? ibH     : na, "IB High",     color = color.new(color.teal,  0), linewidth = 2, style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(liveDay  ? ibL     : na, "IB Low",      color = color.new(color.teal,  0), linewidth = 2, style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(liveTrad ? ePrice  : na, "Entry",       color = color.new(color.blue,  0), linewidth = 1, style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(liveTrad ? curStop : na, "Stop loss",   color = color.new(color.red,   0), linewidth = 1, style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(liveTrad ? tPrice  : na, "Take profit", color = color.new(color.green, 0), linewidth = 1, style = plot.style_linebr)

bgcolor(inIB and showLevels ? color.new(color.teal, 92) : na, title = "IB window")

plotshape(justFilled and inLong,  title = "Long entry",  style = shape.triangleup,   location = location.belowbar, color = color.new(color.green, 0), size = size.small, text = "IB")
plotshape(justFilled and inShort, title = "Short entry", style = shape.triangledown, location = location.abovebar, color = color.new(color.red,   0), size = size.small, text = "IB")

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Statistics table (with a diagnostic row, because a silent zero-trade backtest is the
// single most common way this kind of strategy wastes an afternoon)
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
f_money(float x) =>
    (x < 0 ? "-$" : "$") + str.tostring(math.abs(x), "0.00")

var table st = table.new(position.top_right, 2, 8, border_width = 1, frame_width = 1, frame_color = color.new(color.gray, 50))

var int ibDays = 0
if ibClosed
    ibDays += 1

if showTable and barstate.islast
    int closed = strategy.closedtrades
    float winRt = closed > 0 ? 100.0 * strategy.wintrades / closed : 0.0
    float pf = na
    if strategy.grossloss > 0
        pf := strategy.grossprofit / strategy.grossloss
    float ddPct = strategy.initial_capital > 0 ? 100.0 * strategy.max_drawdown / strategy.initial_capital : 0.0
    color npCol = strategy.netprofit >= 0 ? color.new(color.green, 0) : color.new(color.red, 0)

    // Diagnostic: say why there is nothing to show, rather than showing an empty table.
    string diag  = ""
    color  diagC = color.new(color.gray, 0)
    if ibDays == 0
        diag  := "No IB window found — check the chart timeframe and that the symbol trades 09:30 ET"
        diagC := color.new(color.red, 0)
    else if timeframe.in_seconds() > 900
        diag  := "Timeframe " + timeframe.period + " is too coarse to measure the IB — use 1–5m"
        diagC := color.new(color.orange, 0)
    else if closed == 0
        diag  := "IB found on " + str.tostring(ibDays) + " days but 0 trades — check Properties → Margin"
        diagC := color.new(color.orange, 0)
    else
        diag  := str.tostring(ibDays) + " IB days · " + syminfo.ticker + " · " + f_money(syminfo.pointvalue) + "/pt"

    table.cell(st, 0, 0, "IB backtest",    text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.teal, 20), text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(st, 1, 0, timeframe.period, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.teal, 20), text_size = size.small)

    table.cell(st, 0, 1, "Net profit",   text_size = size.small, text_color = color.gray)
    table.cell(st, 1, 1, f_money(strategy.netprofit), text_size = size.small, text_color = npCol)

    table.cell(st, 0, 2, "Win rate",     text_size = size.small, text_color = color.gray)
    table.cell(st, 1, 2, str.tostring(winRt, "#.##") + "%", text_size = size.small)

    table.cell(st, 0, 3, "Profit factor", text_size = size.small, text_color = color.gray)
    table.cell(st, 1, 3, na(pf) ? "—" : str.tostring(pf, "#.###"), text_size = size.small)

    table.cell(st, 0, 4, "Trades",       text_size = size.small, text_color = color.gray)
    table.cell(st, 1, 4, str.tostring(closed), text_size = size.small)

    table.cell(st, 0, 5, "Max drawdown", text_size = size.small, text_color = color.gray)
    table.cell(st, 1, 5, f_money(strategy.max_drawdown) + " (" + str.tostring(ddPct, "#.#") + "%)", text_size = size.small)

    table.cell(st, 0, 6, "Instrument",   text_size = size.small, text_color = color.gray)
    table.cell(st, 1, 6, syminfo.type,   text_size = size.small)

    table.cell(st, 0, 7, diag, text_size = size.tiny, text_color = diagC)
    table.cell(st, 1, 7, "",   text_size = size.tiny)

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// SOURCE NOTES — what is verified vs. what is a modelling choice
//
// Verified from edgeful's public writing (blog posts on the initial balance breakout
// strategy, the GC initial-balance algo, the YM initial balance strategy, and the IB
// breakeven stop algo):
//   • IB = high/low of the first hour of the NY session, 9:30–10:30 ET.
//   • Wait for the first hour to close before trading.
//   • A "single break" day breaks only one side; edgeful cites ~82% single-break on NQ.
//   • Entry is NOT the breakout itself — it is a retracement back into the range, at 25%
//     of the IB distance inside the range. ("if the IB range is 40 and breaks to the
//     downside, place an entry 10 above the low of the IB range")
//   • Stop loss at 60% of the IB range. ("if the IB range is 40 and the breakout is lower,
//     the stop loss will be set at 24 above the IB low")
//   • Target 50% of the IB range from the broken edge.
//   • One trade per day; if neither stop nor target is hit, exit at the close of trading.
//   • Breakeven-stop management exists as a separate published variant.
//
// Modelling choices made here (NOT edgeful specifications — all are inputs you can change):
//   • The trade window ends at 15:55 ET and flattens; edgeful says "close of trading"
//     without naming a minute.
//   • Break confirmation is a simple wick through the level. Whether edgeful requires a
//     candle CLOSE beyond the edge is not stated in the public posts.
//   • Bar-close order submission: if a break and its retracement complete inside one bar,
//     that entry is missed. This is conservative and avoids intrabar lookahead.
//   • If one bar breaks both sides, the bar's close direction decides.
//   • edgeful's own reports layer probability filters (which side broke first, where the
//     first hour closed in its range) on top of this geometry to pick days. Those are
//     subscription data, not public rules, so no day filter is applied here — this
//     measures the raw mechanical edge on every session.
